    [CI]: require a label for test_selector.py without the full suite (#18539)
    
    Put test_selector.py on the src path filter so an unlabeled PR fails
    ci-gate, while ready-precise stays on the precise path. Add a startup
    probe print so this diff can be checked in CI.
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    The precise test script can pass the gate only after being labeled.
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    no
    ### How was this patch tested?
    After the modification, the access control system displays that the
    tagging is successful.
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/8cc9aa5ad350f6f80cf3bebb298d410803ff75a9
    
    ---------
    
    Signed-off-by: shiqiangA <shiqiang15@huawei.com>

diff --git a/.github/workflows/pr_test.yaml b/.github/workflows/pr_test.yaml
index 00759eb65..35b2534ac 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/pr_test.yaml
+++ b/.github/workflows/pr_test.yaml
@@ -163,6 +163,9 @@ jobs:
               - 'tests/e2e/*.sh'
               - 'tools/**'
               - 'CMakeLists.txt'
+              # Requires a run-enabling label, but stays out of ci_pipeline so
+              # ready-precise is not escalated to the full suite.
+              - '.github/workflows/scripts/test_selector.py'
               - '!**/*.md'
               # CI pipeline files: a PR that touches the test selection or
               # execution pipeline itself must run the full suite, because
@@ -170,6 +173,8 @@ jobs:
               # estimated_times.yaml is intentionally omitted: it only
               # affects load-balanced partitioning, not which tests are
               # recommended, so timing-only PRs keep ready-precise.
+              # test_selector.py is listed under src instead: a label is
+              # required, and ready-precise keeps the precise path.
             ci_pipeline:
               - '.github/workflows/pr_test.yaml'
               - '.github/workflows/_selected_tests.yaml'
